      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I understand the existing codes, this test codes seem to be designed for EC test and to fake console UART port only. uart_inject_char() in chip/host/uart.c (or UART_INJECT()) is the one putting characters into (fake) UART RX buffer. In this test, I didn\u0027t use it. Instead I let his test call ec_comm_process_packet() directly. The INPUT_BUFFER_SIZE defined as 16 in chip/host/uart.c was too small for EC-CR50-packet size, and I didn\u0027t want this test too much complicated.",
